A||||3||Blacktree||Iron Duke question: Swapping cyl heads?||||1||
Z||000000||Blacktree||12-17-2001||02:14 PM||||I have an 86 coupe with a siezed engine, but the cyl head was rebuilt just before the engine went kaput. My daily driver is an 87 SE with the 2.5 engine, and I can tell it's in dire need of some cyl head work.<P>So I was thinking... since I have this rebuilt head with zero miles on it sitting on an unusable engine, maybe I could plop it onto my other engine and everything would be hunky-dory. The one thing keeping me from doing this is the fact that in 1987, Pontiac made a bunch of changes to the 2.5 liter engine. I'm not sure if the head from a 1986 engine would be compatible with the 1987 engine.<P>Does anyone know for sure?<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||RedHaze86SD4||12-17-2001||02:31 PM||||I'm not 100% sure on this but I think you can swap them out only thing is depending on what all bolts to the head from 87 you might have to retain the use of some of the 86 equipment. IE computer, wires and intake manifold... But I seen to be thinking everything is adaptable to the head with minimal fuss... Someone else can help more I'm sure. But I still think its a fair swap..<BR> Sorry can't be more acurate<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RHplate.jpg">  Have to make new sig. RedHaze is now Black with a Red Haze :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-17-2001||08:04 PM||||No... you can't put a head from a distributor motor on a DIS motor.<P>We've been thru that.... The intake side is all differant. I don't remember what else. A couple people already tried it. Been awhile since that thread.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
